Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.40,0:00:06.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every Friday, Rahel and Bekele met at\Nthe same small café.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.01,0:00:10.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,She knew exactly how he took his coffee.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.98,0:00:15.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,He knew when her smile was hiding a\Ndifficult day.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.43,0:00:19.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,What she didn’t know was that he loved\Nher.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.40,0:00:26.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,One afternoon, Rahel told him she’d\Naccepted a job in another city.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.41,0:00:30.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Bekele smiled and told her he was proud.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.11,0:00:36.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,That night, he typed, “There’s something\NI’ve wanted to tell you.”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.16,0:00:38.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,His thumb hovered over send.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.44,0:00:41.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,But he deleted the message.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.48,0:00:45.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,He was afraid the truth might change\Ntheir friendship.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.69,0:00:50.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,At the bus station, Rahel admitted she\Nwas scared.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.69,0:00:54.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Bekele picked up her bag and walked\Nbeside her.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.57,0:01:00.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Before boarding, she handed him a small\Npacket of coffee.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.04,0:01:03.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,“So we can still have our Fridays,” she\Nsaid.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.69,0:01:10.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,As the bus pulled away, his phone lit\Nup: “Friday. Same time?”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.83,0:01:15.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Bekele smiled and typed, “I’ll be\Nthere.”
